{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# S3 — Bound journald storage and alarm on journal saturation\n\n## Why\nJournald is a root-volume accumulator because compose services send logs to the host journal. The incident measured journal growth, and aggregate root alarms do not identify journal saturation.\n\n## What\nInstall managed journald configuration such as `/etc/systemd/journald.conf.d/rebar-disk-ceiling.conf` with an explicit persistent journal ceiling (`SystemMaxUse` and, where useful, `SystemKeepFree`). Extend observability to publish journal usage relative to cap and add a dedicated CloudWatch alarm.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: host journald config installation/reload, observability metric, Terraform alarm, runbook text, and tests. Out of scope: changing compose logging driver, review scratch placement, Docker build-cache cap, `/var/tmp`, and container-layer reaping.\n\n## Grounding\n- Current observability publishes only aggregate data/root disk metrics: `infra/scripts/observability.sh:72-90`.\n- Compose uses journald logging blocks in `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`.\n- systemd-journald docs: `SystemMaxUse` controls maximum persistent journal disk usage under `/var/log/journal`, and journald respects the smaller of `SystemMaxUse`/`SystemKeepFree`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Managed journald config sets an explicit disk ceiling and installs idempotently on the Gerrit host.\n- [ ] Observability emits a journald usage/cap metric testable without live CloudWatch.\n- [ ] Terraform adds a dedicated journald saturation alarm wired to SNS.\n- [ ] Runbook documents journal cap, alarm, diagnosis (`journalctl --disk-usage` or equivalent), and safe remediation.\n- [ ] Targeted tests cover generated config, metric emission, and alarm wiring.\n- [ ] Portability criterion: uses systemd-journald native config and local shell/Python tests; no provider-specific CI trigger is required."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788376362610502406,"uuid":"41c57153-f0ea-461b-9390-bf7675bdc13a"}